        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>two cases are currently supported by the code 1) twophase with gravity on the ELEMENT 2) singlephase with gravity on the ELEMENT_INTEGRATION_POINT</para>
<para>projection of a vector g(0,-1,0) onto a vector r(r[0],r[1],r[2]) (where |r|=1) is equal to (r, g)r = -r[1] r</para>
<para>r*=(r[1]&gt;0.0?-1:1) Note that the direction of the gravity force should be oriented downwards</para>
<para>projection of vector g(0,-1, 0) onto a surface with a normal vector n(n[0], n[1], n[2]) (where |n|=1) is equal to n x (n x g) = (n, g) n - g = -n[1] n - g <linebreak/>
</para>
<para>n*=(n[1]&gt;0.0?-1:1) Note that the direction of the gravity force should be oriented downwards</para>
        </inbodydescription>
